# Example policy grants for SHADOW-AI Shadow Acts (v0.3).
#
# This file is documentation only. The node loads policy from
# `policy.yaml` next to main.py when it exists
# (SHADOW_POLICY_FILE env overrides the path); otherwise it runs on the
# built-in defaults, under which Shadow Acts are HELD for approval and
# never auto-run.
#
# To grant a Shadow Act standing autonomy, copy this file to
# `policy.yaml` and uncomment the grants you want. Each grant is an
# explicit operator decision; removing a line revokes that act's
# autonomy. Grants waive only the approval requirement: emergency pause,
# blocked tools, and destructive double-confirmation still apply.
#
# tool_tiers:
#   # Digest of Google Calendar events starting in the next 24h,
#   # delivered through the node's own notification path.
#   "shadow_act:upcoming_events_brief": "auto_approve"
#   # Digest of reminders due in the next 24h, same notify path.
#   "shadow_act:due_reminders_digest": "auto_approve"
#   # Read-only ambient health report. Never notifies, never writes.
#   "shadow_act:ambient_health": "auto_approve"
